<title>FINLAND: HACKMAN SELLS HAVI UNIT FOR FIM 82 MLN.</title>
<headline>HACKMAN SELLS HAVI UNIT FOR FIM 82 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish consumer goods group Oy Hackman Ab said a statement on Tuesday it had sold its technochemicals unit Hackman Havi Oy to German chemicals group Henkel KGaA for 82 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal means that the Henkel Group (buys) 99.9 percent of the shares in Hackman Havi Oy Ab for a price of 82 million markka,&quot; Hackman said.</p>
<p>The properties in Vantaa and Riihimaki were not included in the deal, it added.</p>
<p>Hackman Havi Oy Ab's name had been changed to Henkel Finland Oy Ab as of March 3, Hackman said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240, news@Reuters.fi</p>
</text>
